From 3c369d4f92a4a54d75df8002ef5ac3855cc869fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Orsavio P. Delmare" <orsavio@delmare.lu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:45:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/50] docs: separate "which slot boots" from "which board it
 is"

Second pass. My previous version argued the ECW336's board from machid and a
CDT subtype, concluding hk01.c6. That is not the selection mechanism and the
unit does not boot that slot.

The actual structure is more useful for this port. machid picks a config
slot; the slot's name says nothing about the board, because each vendor
writes its own board content into whichever slot its hardware matches. The
ECW336 demonstrates it cleanly: it boots the slot named hk07, whose DTB even
carries model = "...IPQ8074/AP-HK07", and yet declares
compatible = qcom,ipq8074-ap-hk01-c6, qcom,ipq8074-hk01. The board is
AP-HK01-C6, an HK host plus a Pine/QCN9074 6 GHz card. Qualcomm's own
firmware_rdp_feature.ini inside the ECW336's wifi-firmware volume confirms it
with a "#HK01-C6 - Pine RDPs : Pine6G + HK(2G+5G) in HK01 platform" section
and no ap-hk07 entry at all.

So the rule is: read the DTB's compatible. Never the slot name, never model
-- that AP-HK07 string appears in the EWS377-FIT's DTB too -- and never the
FIT default. compatible is what OpenWrt board_detect consumes.

Blocker 1 is restated to match: printenv still tells you which slot boots and
should be expected to match the EWS377 units, after which the slot's DTB must
be dumped and its compatible read to learn the board.

Added the measured consequence, which is the part that would have bitten a
port: the ECW336's hk07-slot DTB differs from the EWS377-FIT's by roughly 670
of 3347 lines -- ethernet dp4+dp5 rather than dp5+dp6, ieee802.3-c45 refs for
an Aquantia 10G PHY the EWS377 lacks, ECW336-only aqr_int/dc_det GPIOs, a
wlan_6g_led. Same slot, not interchangeable board DTSs. NSS/EDMA work carries
across since the SoC and NSS clock tree match; the board DTS does not.
